{
  "Name": "Tektronix 2230 (pre-SCPI \"codes\" protocol - NOT IEEE-488.2/SCPI compliant; see docs/design/proposals/tektronix-2230-protocol.md)",
  "Terminator": "\r",
  "Notes": "Built from docs/devices/tektronix-2230/programming-manual.md (Option 12, RS-232-C only). Terminator is set by a physical PARAMETERS DIP switch (section 8), read once at power-up - not by a software command; \\r matches switch position 0 (CR only), the more common setting, but the real instrument may be configured for CR-LF instead - verify against the physical switch before assuming. This device does not understand *IDN? (its own identify query is ID?), so it can never be IdnPattern-auto-selected the way real SCPI instruments are. One command per message line only - the source explicitly warns against ';'-chaining multiple commands on RS-232-C (unlike GPIB/Option 10), since the instrument acts on a command as soon as it's recognized rather than waiting for the line terminator. Two real contradictions in the source, unresolved: FLOw's power-on default is stated as both OFF (prose) and ON (table) - query FLOw? before assuming; REMote's power-on default is stated as OFF (prose) but the table's bracket notation implies ON - query REMote? before sending any state-changing command. Binary curve transfers (CURVe write direction) are not exposed here - they need a raw %<len><binary><checksum> blob impractical for a generic templated command; CURVe? (query/read direction) is exposed since its reply is just text-renderable bytes. REFFrom/REFDisp/REFProt/SAVeref 'lettered' (REF A-Z) forms take a free-text single-letter parameter rather than 26 enumerated commands.",
